&lt;p&gt;Most "free" expense tracking apps on the Play Store and App Store share the same problem: &lt;strong&gt;bloat and ad spam&lt;/strong&gt;. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You open the app just to log a ₹20 cup of chai or a ₹150 auto ride, and you are hit with full-screen personal loan banners, credit card pop-ups, and multi-step forms. After three days, you stop logging altogether.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;To solve this for my own daily spending, I built &lt;strong&gt;Daily House Expense Tracker Pro&lt;/strong&gt;—a lightweight, 100% ad-free Progressive Web App (PWA) designed to log micro-spends in under &lt;strong&gt;3 seconds&lt;/strong&gt; and send an automated summary email every night.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;🔗 &lt;strong&gt;Try it live (no app store download needed):&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://daily-house-expense-trackerpro.firebaseapp.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Daily House Expense Tracker Pro&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;




