&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The last two rows belong to the agent SDK, &lt;code&gt;a2ui-agent-sdk&lt;/code&gt; 0.11.0, which ships with the 1.0 protocol. The sections below take the changes one at a time: what 0.9 did, what 1.0 does, and what it buys.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h4&gt;


  Change 1 — A Whole Surface in One Message
&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;On 0.9&lt;/strong&gt; a new surface took three messages: &lt;code&gt;createSurface&lt;/code&gt; named the catalog, &lt;code&gt;updateComponents&lt;/code&gt; sent the components, and &lt;code&gt;updateDataModel&lt;/code&gt; filled in the data. The renderer held an empty surface until the last one arrived.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;On 1.0&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;createSurface&lt;/code&gt; carries &lt;code&gt;components&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;dataModel&lt;/code&gt; inline. This Express block, a form with a bound text field, a check and a button, compiles to both versions with the SDK's own compiler:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;surface("main")
$/user/name = "Ada"
title = Text(formatString("Hello ${/user/name}"))
btn = Button(Text("Save"), action=Event("save", {name: $/user/name}, userMessage="Saving"))
root = Column([title, TextField("Name", $/user/name, checks=[?required("Name is required")]), btn])
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;





&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;python3 docs/a2ui-1-0/tools/express_0_9_vs_1_0.py
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;





&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;## A2UI 1.0: 1 message(s): ['createSurface']
## A2UI 0.9 (userMessage removed): 3 message(s): ['createSurface', 'updateComponents', 'updateDataModel']
## userMessage on 0.9
ExpressValidationError: Event userMessage requires protocol v1.0 or later; the target version v0.9 has no userMessage field.
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why it is better:&lt;/strong&gt; the renderer has everything it needs to draw the surface from the first message, and there is no ordering between three messages to get wrong. Updates still use &lt;code&gt;updateComponents&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;updateDataModel&lt;/code&gt; once a surface exists.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h4&gt;


  Change 2 — The Model Writes Express, Not JSON
&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;On 0.9&lt;/strong&gt; the model wrote A2UI JSON into its reply, inside &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;a2ui-json&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; tags. The 0.9 build's &lt;code&gt;page.tsx&lt;/code&gt; cut the blocks out of the text with regular expressions, and a &lt;code&gt;normalizeA2UIJson&lt;/code&gt; function repaired the shapes the model produced before handing them to the renderer.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;On 1.0&lt;/strong&gt; the SDK's default output format is Express: a short Python-like language inside &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;a2ui&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; tags. &lt;code&gt;$/path&lt;/code&gt; is a binding, &lt;code&gt;?required&lt;/code&gt; is a check, &lt;code&gt;root =&lt;/code&gt; names the top component, and arguments follow the catalog's signatures. The SDK generates the prompt from the catalogs, compiles the block on the server, validates it against the catalog, and sends the JSON. Here is the rate card in Express:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;surface("main")
root__text_1 = Text("### 100.00 USD = 89.87 EUR")
root__text_2 = Text("1 USD = 0.89871 EUR")
root__divider_1 = Divider()
root__text_3 = Text("ECB reference rate for 2026-11-11 (Frankfurter API)", "caption")
root__column_1 = Column([root__text_1, root__text_2, root__divider_1, root__text_3])
root = Card(root__column_1)
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The same six components as 0.9 JSON:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;[{"version":"v0.9","createSurface":{"surfaceId":"main","catalogId":"https://a2ui.org/catalog/currency-charts"}},{"version":"v0.9","updateComponents":{"surfaceId":"main","components":[{"component":"Text","id":"root__text_1","text":"100.00 USD = 89.87 EUR","variant":"h3"},{"component":"Text","id":"root__text_2","text":"1 USD = 0.89871 EUR"},{"component":"Divider","id":"root__divider_1"},{"component":"Text","id":"root__text_3","text":"ECB reference rate for 2026-11-11 (Frankfurter API)","variant":"caption"},{"component":"Column","id":"root__column_1","children":["root__text_1","root__text_2","root__divider_1","root__text_3"]},{"component":"Card","id":"root","child":"root__column_1"}]}}]
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why it is better:&lt;/strong&gt; the model writes fewer tokens (139 against 223 for this card, table below), and a malformed block fails on the server, before anything reaches a browser: the tool returns the compiler's error to the model in its result. The browser receives JSON that has already passed the catalog's schema, so the 1.0 &lt;code&gt;page.tsx&lt;/code&gt; has no parser and no normalizer: it went from 309 lines to 150.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h4&gt;


  Change 3 — Server-Side Macros: Figures Never Pass Through the Model
&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;On 0.9&lt;/strong&gt; the model called the rate tool, read the result, and typed every figure into the component JSON. A history chart meant the model copying 64 dates and 64 rates back out.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;On 1.0&lt;/strong&gt; a macro is a Python function the model calls like a component. &lt;code&gt;@macro&lt;/code&gt; turns its type hints and docstring into an entry in a separate macros catalog that only the model sees. At send time &lt;code&gt;MacroExpander&lt;/code&gt; runs the function and replaces the call with Basic catalog components, so the browser needs no macro support. From &lt;code&gt;currency_agent/macros.py&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nd"&gt;@macro&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;RateCard&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;currency_from&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;currency_to&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;amount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;float&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mf"&gt;1.0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"""Card with the live exchange rate and a converted amount. The server looks
    up the rate, so do not pass rate figures.
    """&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;src&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;dst&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;_code&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;currency_from&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;_code&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;currency_to&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;_get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"latest"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;**&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"from"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;src&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"to"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;dst&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;rate&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"rates"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;dst&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;child&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Column&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="n"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
                &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Text&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;text&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"### {amount:,.2f} {src} = {amount * rate:,.2f} {dst}"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
                &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Text&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;text&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"1 {src} = {rate:.5f} {dst}"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
                &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Divider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
                &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Text&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
                    &lt;span class="n"&gt;text&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"ECB reference rate for {data['date']} (Frankfurter API)"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
                    &lt;span class="n"&gt;variant&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"caption"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
                &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;For "Convert 100 USD to EUR please." the model's whole tool call was:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;a2ui&amp;gt;
surface("conversion")
root = RateCard("USD", "EUR", 100)
&amp;lt;/a2ui&amp;gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;What reached the browser:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;version 1.0, ['createSurface'], 6 components
  https://a2ui.org/specification/v1_0/catalogs/basic/catalog.json: ['Text', 'Text', 'Divider', 'Text', 'Column', 'Card']
  Text: ### 100.00 USD = 89.87 EUR
  Text: 1 USD = 0.89871 EUR
  Text: ECB reference rate for 2026-11-11 (Frankfurter API)
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The agent validates twice: once against the catalogs the model sees, which include the macros, and again after expansion against the catalogs the browser implements:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;_parse_payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;processor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;messages&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;super&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;_parse_payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;processor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;typed&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;_message_adapter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;validate_python&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;m&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;m&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;messages&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;expanded&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;macro_expander&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;transform_to_transport&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;typed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;wire&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;m&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;model_dump&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;by_alias&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;True&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;exclude_none&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;True&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;m&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;expanded&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nf"&gt;validate_payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;BASE_CATALOGS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;wire&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;wire&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why it is better:&lt;/strong&gt; the figures come from the source on the server, so the model cannot mistype a rate, and data the model does not need to see stays out of its context. The model's output stops growing with the data: the 90-day chart is 21 tokens as a macro call against 1,060 as 0.9 JSON. Macro arguments come from the model, so &lt;code&gt;_code()&lt;/code&gt; accepts only a three-letter currency code and day counts are clamped to 7–365.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fwc1ncjb6xlly4n6bgm61.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fwc1ncjb6xlly4n6bgm61.png" alt="Line chart of USD to JPY from 2026-08-13 to 2026-11-11 with low 153.27, high 160.16 and latest 159.23" width="800" height="760"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h4&gt;


  How Many Tokens Does the Model Write?
&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;docs/a2ui-1-0/tools/token_cost.py&lt;/code&gt; builds three answers once with live rates, writes each in four forms, and counts every form with the Gemini &lt;code&gt;countTokens&lt;/code&gt; API:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;python3 docs/a2ui-1-0/tools/token_cost.py gemini-2.5-flash
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;





&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;# Tokens the model writes for the same UI, counted by gemini-2.5-flash countTokens
| Answer | Components | 0.9 JSON | 1.0 JSON | 1.0 Express | 1.0 macro |
| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| Rate card | 6 | 223 | 212 | 139 | 21 |
| 90-day chart | 5 | 1060 | 1152 | 1101 | 21 |
| 3-currency comparison | 8 | 347 | 522 | 253 | 22 |
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;gemini-3.8-flash&lt;/code&gt; counted the same numbers. Two things the table shows:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Express shrinks structure.&lt;/strong&gt; On the card and the comparison, where most tokens are component structure, Express is the smallest form the model can write by hand. On the chart, where most tokens are 64 dates and 64 rates, every hand-written form costs about the same.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Macros remove the data.&lt;/strong&gt; A macro call costs the same 21 or 22 tokens whatever it expands to.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The 1.0 JSON for the comparison is the largest form because it mixes two catalogs, so each component names its own &lt;code&gt;catalogId&lt;/code&gt; (Change 4). Express leaves catalog ids out and the compiler fills them in.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h4&gt;


  Change 4 — Several Catalogs on One Surface
&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;On 0.9&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;createSurface&lt;/code&gt; named one catalog id, and every component on the surface came from it. The 0.9 build loaded Basic 0.9 and its charts catalog, &lt;code&gt;https://a2ui.org/catalog/currency-charts&lt;/code&gt;, through &lt;code&gt;A2uiSchemaManager&lt;/code&gt;, which selected one catalog for the surface.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;On 1.0&lt;/strong&gt; each component can name its own &lt;code&gt;catalogId&lt;/code&gt;. The browser here implements Basic 1.0 and a currency charts catalog with &lt;code&gt;LineChart&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;BarChart&lt;/code&gt;. For "Show me EUR to USD for the past 6 months and the current rate" the model wrote two macro calls:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;a2ui&amp;gt;
surface("main")
root = Column([rateCard, historyChart])
rateCard = RateCard("EUR", "USD")
historyChart = RateHistoryChart("EUR", "USD", 180)
&amp;lt;/a2ui&amp;gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The browser received one &lt;code&gt;createSurface&lt;/code&gt; with each component naming its catalog:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;version 1.0, ['createSurface'], 12 components
  https://a2ui.org/specification/v1_0/catalogs/basic/catalog.json: ['Column', 'Text', 'Text', 'Divider', 'Text', 'Column', 'Card', 'Text', 'Text', 'Column', 'Card']
  https://a2ui.org/catalog/currency-charts/v1/catalog.json: ['LineChart']
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fg1h3ecw97kcbvzdibb5u.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fg1h3ecw97kcbvzdibb5u.png" alt="A rate card for EUR to USD above a 180-day line chart" width="800" height="1019"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why it is better:&lt;/strong&gt; a custom catalog holds only the custom components, &lt;code&gt;LineChart&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;BarChart&lt;/code&gt; here, and sits beside the standard Basic catalog on the same surface. The charts catalog is now &lt;code&gt;https://a2ui.org/catalog/currency-charts/v1/catalog.json&lt;/code&gt; with &lt;code&gt;protocolVersion&lt;/code&gt; 1.0, and its id and props match between &lt;code&gt;currency_agent/custom_catalog.json&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;A2UICustomCatalog.tsx&lt;/code&gt; in the browser.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h4&gt;


  Change 5 — The UI Arrives as a Tool Result
&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;On 0.9&lt;/strong&gt; the UI travelled inside the reply text. CopilotKit's A2UI middleware and &lt;code&gt;@copilotkit/a2ui-renderer&lt;/code&gt; read it, and the 0.9 build's AG-UI checks searched the final text for &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;a2ui-json&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; tags.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;On 1.0&lt;/strong&gt; the model passes its Express block to the &lt;code&gt;send_a2ui_json_to_client&lt;/code&gt; tool, and the tool result carries the validated messages in &lt;code&gt;validated_a2ui_json&lt;/code&gt;. The page registers a renderer for that tool and hands the messages to &lt;code&gt;@a2ui/react&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useRenderTool&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"send_a2ui_json_to_client"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;render&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;any&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;messages&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;extractA2uiMessages&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;messages&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;A2uiMessages&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;messages&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;messages&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;any&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why it is better:&lt;/strong&gt; the UI travels separately from the chat text, so a reply can mix prose and a card without the browser guessing where one ends. CopilotKit's built-in A2UI middleware speaks 0.9, so it is switched off in &lt;code&gt;route.ts&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fs9odz4whycal1p6rj7bi.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fs9odz4whycal1p6rj7bi.png" alt="1 USD against 3 currencies: today's rates for EUR, GBP and CHF above a bar chart of the change since 2026-10-12, EUR up 0.49 percent, GBP down 0.54, CHF down 0.36" width="800" height="970"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h4&gt;


  Change 6 — Breaking Changes to Plan For
&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;p&gt;These need edits when moving a 0.9 agent or renderer to 1.0:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Headings come from Markdown.&lt;/strong&gt; Text's &lt;code&gt;h1&lt;/code&gt;–&lt;code&gt;h5&lt;/code&gt; variants are gone; &lt;code&gt;caption&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;body&lt;/code&gt; remain, and Text renders Markdown. The macros write &lt;code&gt;### 250.00 USD = 224.68 EUR&lt;/code&gt; for the headline line, and &lt;code&gt;@a2ui/react&lt;/code&gt; renders it with &lt;code&gt;@a2ui/markdown-it&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;theme&lt;/code&gt; is gone from &lt;code&gt;createSurface&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Bindings and calls are prefixed:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;{"path": ...}&lt;/code&gt; is &lt;code&gt;{"@path": ...}&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;{"call": ...}&lt;/code&gt; is &lt;code&gt;{"@call": ...}&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The version string is &lt;code&gt;"1.0"&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, without the &lt;code&gt;v&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Component props moved:&lt;/strong&gt; TextField gains &lt;code&gt;placeholder&lt;/code&gt; and replaces &lt;code&gt;validationRegexp&lt;/code&gt; with a &lt;code&gt;regex&lt;/code&gt; check, Slider gains &lt;code&gt;steps&lt;/code&gt;, and Video gains &lt;code&gt;posterUrl&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;h4&gt;


  Change 7 — What 1.0 Adds
&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;p&gt;From the 1.0 schemas in &lt;code&gt;a2ui-core&lt;/code&gt; 0.6.0:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Functions in both directions.&lt;/strong&gt; The agent can call a renderer function (&lt;code&gt;callRendererFunction&lt;/code&gt;) and the renderer can call an agent function (&lt;code&gt;callAgentFunction&lt;/code&gt;), each with its own response message.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Function permissions.&lt;/strong&gt; A catalog marks each function &lt;code&gt;rendererOnly&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;agentOnly&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;rendererOrAgent&lt;/code&gt;, and can require a user gesture with &lt;code&gt;requiresUserActivation&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Composition rules.&lt;/strong&gt; A catalog can list &lt;code&gt;allowedParents&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;allowedChildren&lt;/code&gt; per component, and the renderer reports violations with the error codes &lt;code&gt;UNALLOWED_PARENT&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;UNALLOWED_CHILD&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Graded validation.&lt;/strong&gt; Checks return a result with a &lt;code&gt;severity&lt;/code&gt; of error, warning or info.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Actions that speak.&lt;/strong&gt; A button's action can carry a &lt;code&gt;userMessage&lt;/code&gt;, which travels with the action to the agent. The compiler rejects it on 0.9, as Change 1 shows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Accessibility.&lt;/strong&gt; Components take &lt;code&gt;live&lt;/code&gt; (off, polite, assertive) and &lt;code&gt;hidden&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;List positions.&lt;/strong&gt; The &lt;code&gt;@index&lt;/code&gt; function returns an item's position inside a list template.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Extensions.&lt;/strong&gt; Components, surfaces, actions and catalogs carry &lt;code&gt;metadata.extensions&lt;/code&gt; for custom data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Catalog instructions.&lt;/strong&gt; A catalog can carry Markdown &lt;code&gt;instructions&lt;/code&gt; for the model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;h4&gt;


  Does It Hold Up?
&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fkm49gmbyjfctzebrov8h.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fkm49gmbyjfctzebrov8h.png" alt="Before and after: on A2UI 0.9 the model calls the rate tool and writes the component JSON with the figures, the reply text carries a2ui-json blocks, and the browser cuts them out and repairs them; on A2UI 1.0 the model writes one macro call, the server compiles and validates it, the macro fetches the rate, the result is validated again and arrives as a tool result" width="798" height="238"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;docs/a2ui-1-0/tools/render_suite.py&lt;/code&gt; sends ten prompts ten times each through Next.js. A UI prompt passes when the reply rendered A2UI and no raw &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;a2ui&lt;/code&gt; text reached the chat; the weather question passes as text with no UI.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;python3 docs/a2ui-1-0/tools/render_suite.py 10 gemini-3.8-flash render-suite-gemini-3.8-flash.jsonl
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;





&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;# gemini-3.8-flash: 100 of 100 replies rendered clean (10 runs per prompt)
10 of 10: pass | Compare 1 USD in EUR, GBP, JPY and CAD
10 of 10: pass | Compare the euro, pound and Swiss franc against the dollar in a bar chart
10 of 10: pass | Convert 100 USD to XYZ
10 of 10: pass | How much is 250 USD in EUR?
10 of 10: pass | Show a bar chart of 1 USD in EUR, GBP, JPY, CHF and CAD
10 of 10: pass | Show me EUR to USD for the past 6 months and the current rate
10 of 10: pass | Show me the USD to JPY trend over the last 90 days
10 of 10: pass | What's a thousand euros in dollars?
10 of 10: pass | What's the weather in Paris?
10 of 10: pass | Write the A2UI block for a USD to EUR rate card directly in your reply text. Do not call any tool.
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;





&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;# gemini-2.5-flash: 100 of 100 replies rendered clean (10 runs per prompt)
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Every comparison reply on both models came from the &lt;code&gt;RateComparison&lt;/code&gt; macro, with no call to the rate tool:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;## gemini-2.5-flash
10 of 10: no rate-tool call, BarChart=True | Compare 1 USD in EUR, GBP, JPY and CAD
10 of 10: no rate-tool call, BarChart=True | Compare the euro, pound and Swiss franc against the dol
10 of 10: no rate-tool call, BarChart=True | Show a bar chart of 1 USD in EUR, GBP, JPY, CHF and CAD
## gemini-3.8-flash
10 of 10: no rate-tool call, BarChart=True | Compare 1 USD in EUR, GBP, JPY and CAD
10 of 10: no rate-tool call, BarChart=True | Compare the euro, pound and Swiss franc against the dol
10 of 10: no rate-tool call, BarChart=True | Show a bar chart of 1 USD in EUR, GBP, JPY, CHF and CAD
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;






&lt;h4&gt;


  🔎 Tip: Express Is a Format, Not a Python Feature
&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The A2UI repository ships YAML conformance suites for the Express compiler and the response parser, tagged with the &lt;code&gt;a2ui-agent-sdk&lt;/code&gt; 0.11.0 release. A Rust port of the same agent, &lt;a href="https://github.com/xbill9/currency-agent-rust-agui-a2ui1" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://github.com/xbill9/currency-agent-rust-agui-a2ui1&lt;/a&gt;, implements Express and server-side macros in Rust and runs them:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;cargo &lt;span class="nb"&gt;test&lt;/span&gt; --test express_conformance -- --nocapture
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;





&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;agent/express/response_parser.yaml: 38/38 passed, 0 known gaps, 0 failed
agent/express/compiler.yaml: 132/135 passed, 3 known gaps, 0 failed
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The three compiler cases it skips use a 0.9 catalog; the port targets 1.0 only.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h4&gt;


  🔎 Tip: Keep the Macros Catalog on the Model's Side
&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The macros sit in a catalog that exists only for the model: &lt;code&gt;macro_expander.transform_catalogs(BASE_CATALOGS)&lt;/code&gt; adds it to the prompt and the compiler. The browser's catalogs stay Basic 1.0 plus charts, and the second validation pass confirms every component the browser receives belongs to one of them.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h4&gt;


  At This Point You Should Have…
&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Python 3.13 or newer and Node.js with npm&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Gemini API key from Google AI Studio, or a Google Cloud project with Vertex AI enabled&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The repository cloned:
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;git clone https://github.com/xbill9/currency-claude-agui-a2ui1.git
&lt;span class="nb"&gt;cd&lt;/span&gt; currency-claude-agui-a2ui1
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;






&lt;h4&gt;


  Step 1 — Install and Configure
&lt;/h4&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;make install
&lt;span class="nb"&gt;echo&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"GOOGLE_API_KEY=&amp;lt;your_api_key_here&amp;gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; .env
&lt;span class="nb"&gt;echo&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"GOOGLE_GENAI_USE_VERTEXAI=FALSE"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; .env
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;make install&lt;/code&gt; runs &lt;code&gt;uv sync&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;npm install&lt;/code&gt; for both front ends. The agent uses &lt;code&gt;gemini-3.8-flash&lt;/code&gt; unless &lt;code&gt;GENAI_MODEL&lt;/code&gt; is set in &lt;code&gt;.env&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h4&gt;


  Step 2 — Start the Stack and Ask
&lt;/h4&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;make start
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:10000/health
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8008/health
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;





&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;{"status":"ok"}
{"status":"ok"}
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Open &lt;a href="http://localhost:3000" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;http://localhost:3000&lt;/a&gt; and ask &lt;strong&gt;How much is 250 USD in EUR?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Ffjhttf83628hs220ovsa.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Ffjhttf83628hs220ovsa.png" alt="Rate card: 250.00 USD = 224.68 EUR, 1 USD = 0.89871 EUR, ECB reference rate for 2026-11-11" width="800" height="421"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h4&gt;


  Compare and Contrast
&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The same answers on each version, tokens counted by &lt;code&gt;gemini-2.5-flash&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;A2UI 0.9&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;A2UI 1.0, Express&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;A2UI 1.0, macro 🥇&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Rate card&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;223 tokens&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;139 tokens&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;21 tokens&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;90-day chart&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;1,060 tokens&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;1,101 tokens&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;21 tokens&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;3-currency comparison&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;347 tokens&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;253 tokens&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;22 tokens&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Messages per new surface&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;3&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Figures typed by&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;the model&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;the model&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;the server&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
