&lt;h2&gt;


  FAQ
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Do I need a configuration flag to use ViewTransition in Next.js?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Not on Next.js 16.4 or later. The view transitions guide and the documentation bundled with &lt;code&gt;next@16.4.5&lt;/code&gt; say view transitions work in the App Router with no configuration, because React 19.3 provides &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;ViewTransition&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;addTransitionType&lt;/code&gt;. Older 16.x versions documented an &lt;code&gt;experimental.viewTransition&lt;/code&gt; flag, so check the docs in &lt;code&gt;node_modules/next/dist/docs&lt;/code&gt; for your installed version.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Why does my ViewTransition not animate?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The most common causes are an update that is not wrapped in &lt;code&gt;startTransition&lt;/code&gt;, a DOM element placed above the boundary, a boundary inside a layout that never enters or exits, and &lt;code&gt;default="none"&lt;/code&gt; on a shared pair without an explicit &lt;code&gt;share&lt;/code&gt; prop. A &lt;code&gt;flushSync&lt;/code&gt; call during the update also makes React skip the animation. None of these produces an error.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Does React ViewTransition work in Firefox and Safari?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The core View Transitions API has been supported in all major browser engines since October 2025. React's integration also uses transition types and &lt;code&gt;view-transition-class&lt;/code&gt;, which Next.js lists as available in Chromium 125 and later and in recent Safari and Firefox versions. Where support is missing, the app works normally and simply does not animate.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Does React turn off View Transitions for reduced motion?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;No. React does not check the user's motion preference. Add a &lt;code&gt;prefers-reduced-motion&lt;/code&gt; media query that sets animation durations and delays to zero on the &lt;code&gt;::view-transition-old&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;::view-transition-new&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;::view-transition-group&lt;/code&gt; pseudo-elements, or keep only opacity changes and remove movement.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Can I use ViewTransition with React Native?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Not yet. The React 19.3 announcement says &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;ViewTransition&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; currently works only in the DOM, and that support for React Native and other platforms is being worked on. Fragment refs and the other 19.3 changes are separate from this limitation.&lt;/p&gt;




